hod","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1167/jov.22.14.3993","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1167/jov.22.14.3993","citation_count":1,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1167/jov.22.14.3993","url":"https://doi.org/10.1167/jov.22.14.3993","query":"deepfake image detection @ International Journal of Computer Vision","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:44:57Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-115eae5c97ae7dd0","title":"Watermarking for Tamper Detection, Copyright Protection, and Rightful Ownership of a Digital Image: A Literature Survey","title_zh":"","year":2022,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-29ec42fd0126d6","name":"Pavan A C","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-498664c564ae3a","name":"Dr. M.T. Somashekara","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-c21bcf90e69393","name":"SSRN Electronic Journal","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"1556-5068","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"survey","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.2139/ssrn.4304022","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.4304022","citation_count":1,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.2139/ssrn.4304022","url":"https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.4304022","query":"image content credential tamper detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:06:00Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-d4cbb3c48629f5d0","title":"DWT based color image watermarking: a review","title_zh":"","year":2020,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-d7c6a44233c4da","name":"Kaiser J. Giri","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-c74f64ca0a4b95","name":"S. M. K. Quadri","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-4b3a2c79054bf6","name":"Rumaan Bashir","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-1a7ab0c6b9b827","name":"Javaid Iqbal Bhat","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-e43d0ed7069ca7","name":"Multimedia Tools and Applications","short_name":"MTAP","type":"journal","issn":"1380-7501","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["digital_watermarking"],"contribution_type":"survey","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1007/s11042-020-09716-6","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11042-020-09716-6","citation_count":35,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1007/s11042-020-09716-6","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11042-020-09716-6","query":"image watermarking @ ACM Multimedia","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:42:52Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-294aa00a0b7b01d0","title":"Siamese convolutional neural network‐based approach towards universal image forensics","title_zh":"","year":2020,"publication_date":"2020-06-12","abstract":"This study proposes a novel deep learning‐based method which can detect different types of image editing operations carried out on images. Unlike most of the existing methods, which can only detect the editing operations considered in the training stage, the proposed method can generalise to manipulations not seen in the training stage. The method is based on the classification of image pairs as either similarly or differently processed using a deep siamese neural network. Once the network learns features that can discriminate different editing operations, it can check whether an image is processed with an editing operation, not present in the training stage, using the one‐shot classification strategy. An image forgery detection and localisation technique is also proposed using the trained siamese network. The experimental results show the efficacy of the proposed method in detecting different editing operations and also show the ability in detecting and localising image forgeries.","authors":[{"id":"a5103027449","name":"Aniruddha Mazumdar","orcid":"0000-0001-6909-0428","institution_ids":["i1317621060","i4210089896"]},{"id":"a5113576734","name":"Prabin Kumar Bora","orcid":"0009-0005-4283-7014","institution_ids":["i1317621060","i4210089896"]}],"institution_ids":["i1317621060","i4210089896"],"venue":{"id":"venue-9118ab2d554aba","name":"IET Image Processing","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1049/iet-ipr.2019.1114","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W3035070091","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1049/iet-ipr.2019.1114","citation_count":16,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W3035070091","url":"https://openalex.org/W3035070091","query":"image retouching detection forensics","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T03:56:55Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-da6235e2524c46d0","title":"Using of convolutional neural networks for steganalysis of digital images","title_zh":"","year":2020,"publication_date":"2020-01-01","abstract":"The article substantiates the relevance of steganalysis, as a determination of the presence of a hidden channel in telecommunication systems, whose nodes exchange digital images. The article deals with the application of convolutional neural networks to solve this problem. It is assumed that the probability of correct image classification using a well-trained convolutional neural network will be comparable or even better than characteristics of statistical algorithms or the RM model. We introduce principles of construction and capabilities of convolutional neural networks in the framework of their applicability to solving the problem of steganalysis. To improve the efficiency and effectiveness of the stegocontainer recognition process, a version of the image classification model for a convolutional neural network is proposed. It is based on combination of several convolutional and fully connected layers. We have developed software for this model version with the ability to train a neural network and evaluate the quality of classification. The analysis of existing software products designed for the task of determining the fact of using steganography in digital images is carried out. The advantage of classifiers based on neural networks in comparison with statistical ones is proved. Using the developed software, an experimental study of classification model on sets of digital images contained in open sources has been carried out. The article presents the results of neural network training, as well as an analysis of the strengths and weaknesses of the selected model.","authors":[{"id":"a5044647762","name":"Alexander Polunin","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5062085381","name":"Elina Yandashevskaya","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-652258c5ffd32f","name":"Proceedings of the Institute for System Programming of RAS","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"analysis","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.15514/ispras-2020-32(4)-11","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W3092331627","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.15514/ispras-2020-32(4)-11","citation_count":8,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W3092331627","url":"https://openalex.org/W3092331627","query":"deep residual network image steganalysis","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T03:56:55Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-f7db06d76e7a68d0","title":"Competitive Coevolution for Color Image Steganography","title_zh":"","year":2019,"publication_date":"","abstract":"The need for more secure and advanced dissemination is ever increasing since advancement in digital transmission has also posed equally challenging threats. Steganography has been around for a while now, with frequent updates in the traditional methods. In the past one year, with the rise in research in deep learning, Steganography and Steganalysis have emerged as a prime application. The paper has further worked on it, with introducing a competitive coevolution learning approach wherein Generative Adversarial Networks(GANs) are used for performing steganography along with steganalysis to improve the overall results. RGB color images are used as cover and secret images. A mixed loss function was used which is a weighted sum of Mean Squared Error(MSE), Structural Similarity Index(SSIM) and Mean Structural Similarity Index(MSSIM) for generating the stego image and extracting the secret image. The major improvements proposed in this paper are the introduction of attention based Squeeze and Excitation-Inception modules in the hiding and the reveal networks, which enhance spatial encoding and increase the representational power of the network, thereby giving better overall results.","authors":[{"id":"26936801","name":"Sarthak Ahuja","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2244371708","name":"C. Kumar","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2335594747","name":"Hemalatha S","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-8e8a310de31d5f","name":"International Conference on Conceptual Structures","short_name":"","type":"unknown","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/iccs45141.2019.9065844","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"0324d382095b8296120c64b4bf6ffe985caec606","primary_url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/0324d382095b8296120c64b4bf6ffe985caec606","citation_count":2,"provenance":[{"source":"semantic_scholar","source_id":"0324d382095b8296120c64b4bf6ffe985caec606","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/0324d382095b8296120c64b4bf6ffe985caec606","query":"spatial image steganalysis","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T18:33:18Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-b98d2126b83240d0","title":"Maximum Payload for Digital Image Steganography Obtained by Mixed Edge Detection Mechanism","title_zh":"","year":2019,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-4f310bd6dd90c8","name":"Biswajit Jena","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-5af065cc33b8bc","name":"Gopal Krishna Nayak","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-26b49416c37dd5","name":"Sanjay Saxena","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-7e7802afbdabf6","name":"2019 International Conference on Information Technology (ICIT)","short_name":"","type":"conference","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/icit48102.2019.00043","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/icit48102.2019.00043","citation_count":6,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/icit48102.2019.00043","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/icit48102.2019.00043","query":"image steganography detection benchmark","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:06:03Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-8ea75531a2ac6cd0","title":"Image Steganography Using Edge Detection Technique","title_zh":"","year":2018,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-22eaee5d3b1a4b","name":"Kirti Chopra","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-c126f2c9f1098e","name":"Ishpreet Singh Virk","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-1b83c06f0b65c8","name":"International Journal of Computer Sciences and Engineering","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"2347-2693","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.26438/ijcse/v6i12.222227","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.26438/ijcse/v6i12.222227","citation_count":1,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.26438/ijcse/v6i12.222227","url":"https://doi.org/10.26438/ijcse/v6i12.222227","query":"image steganography detection benchmark","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:06:03Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-8002a27e64ae5ad0","title":"A robust technique for splicing detection in tampered blurred images","title_zh":"","year":2017,"publication_date":"2017-05-01","abstract":"Image splicing is a common way of image forgery wherein a part of an image is cropped and pasted to another image. The rapid growth of various image editing softwares has led to the generation of a large number of forged images. Image splicing detection can be made possible by the analysis of a collection of features or characteristics of an image which distinguishes it from an authentic image. Splicing detection can be more challenging if the forger uses some post-processing operations after splicing. After a normal cut and paste of a portion of an image, the composite image so formed can be made to undergo other post-processing operations like blurring of edges, resizing, rotation, noise addition etc. to remove the traces of forgery. The objective of this paper is to develop a technique for splicing detection in case of tampered blurred images in which the original and spliced regions have different blur types. The inconsistencies in the blur types of tampered images are considered for the detection of splicing in these images. The proposed method is also robust to noise attacks.","authors":[{"id":"a5077155092","name":"B Ambili","orcid":"","institution_ids":["i177436651"]},{"id":"a5061462762","name":"Nimmy George","orcid":"0000-0002-0121-4970","institution_ids":["i177436651"]}],"institution_ids":["i177436651"],"venue":{"id":"venue-19e8e71582b170","name":"2017 International Conference on Trends in Electronics and Informatics (ICEI)","short_name":"","type":"conference","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/icoei.2017.8300836","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W2790339174","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/icoei.2017.8300836","citation_count":7,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W2790339174","url":"https://openalex.org/W2790339174","query":"image splicing detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-aadf220f53c956d0","title":"Generative Adversarial Networks for Image Steganography","title_zh":"","year":2017,"publication_date":"2017-04-24","abstract":"Steganography is collection of methods to hide secret information (payload) within non-secret information (container). Its counterpart, Steganalysis, is the practice of determining if a message contains a hidden payload, and recovering it if possible. Presence of hidden payloads is typically detected by a binary classifier. In the present study, we propose a new model for generating image-like containers based on Deep Convolutional Generative Adversarial Networks (DCGAN). This approach allows to generate more setganalysis-secure message embedding using standard steganography algorithms. Experiment results demonstrate that the new model successfully deceives the steganography analyzer, and for this reason, can be used in steganographic applications.","authors":[{"id":"a5002738217","name":"Denis Volkhonskiy","orcid":"0000-0002-9463-7883","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5076875274","name":"Б. Б. Борисенко","orcid":"","institution_ids":["i118501908"]},{"id":"a5088950452","name":"Evgeny Burnaev","orcid":"0000-0001-8424-0690","institution_ids":["i125989756"]}],"institution_ids":["i118501908","i125989756"],"venue":null,"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W2752821911","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=H1hoFU9xe","citation_count":53,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W2752821911","url":"https://openalex.org/W2752821911","query":"adversarial image steganalysis","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T03:56:55Z"},{"source":"semantic_scholar","source_id":"147b7998526ebbdf64b1662503b378d9f6456ccd","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/147b7998526ebbdf64b1662503b378d9f6456ccd","query":"adversarial image steganalysis","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:11:10Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-27f319e9eeddd9d0","title":"Image forgery detection by semi-automatic wavelet soft-Thresholding with error level analysis","title_zh":"","year":2017,"publication_date":"2017-05-20","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"a5040834207","name":"Daniel Cavalcanti Jeronymo","orcid":"0000-0003-3492-4466","institution_ids":["i1283613182"]},{"id":"a5085739192","name":"Yuri Campbell","orcid":"0000-0002-4166-2081","institution_ids":["i4210091327","i4210119712"]},{"id":"a5006394687","name":"Leandro dos Santos Coelho","orcid":"0000-0001-5728-943X","institution_ids":["i1283613182","i176838256","i52418104"]}],"institution_ids":["i1283613182","i176838256","i4210091327","i4210119712","i52418104"],"venue":{"id":"venue-58a6925c7ec42a","name":"Expert Systems with Applications","short_name":"ESWA","type":"journal","issn":"","rankings":[{"system":"CAS","level":"1","category":"计算机科学","scope":"大类","is_top":true,"version":"2025","source_url":"https://www.iikx.com/sci/technology/12439.html","verified_at":"2026-08-12"},{"system":"JCR","level":"Q1","category":"Computer Science; Engineering","scope":"","is_top":false,"version":"2026","source_url":"https://www.iikx.com/sci/technology/12439.html","verified_at":"2026-08-12"}]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"analysis","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1016/j.eswa.2017.05.044","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W2616861335","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eswa.2017.05.044","citation_count":46,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W2616861335","url":"https://openalex.org/W2616861335","query":"image forgery detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-1